From 4a783bae78b44e2b29e3312b16a2e9a032ee312e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:35:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Draw a stage's training history from its ledgers, for one
 run or several

A report-only reader of a stage directory's eval_episodes.csv,
train_episodes.csv, stage_config.json, progress.json and checkpoint
zips (reporting/training_history.py), behind
scripts/plot_training_history.py STAGE_DIR [STAGE_DIR ...] --out DIR.

- Per evaluation: episodes, falls, clean and saturation-flagged
  episodes and the mean return; per foot the whole-foot and pad CoP,
  digit share, toe margin, shear and cone use; sole tilt and corner
  lift; CoM, root pitch and the XcoM margins; the left-minus-right hip
  pitch, knee and ankle offsets; actuator_force_frac_max. Each
  per-episode value over the evaluation's full-horizon episodes.
- Training falls per 262,144-step window of train_episodes.csv.
- The per-actuator policy std, exp(log_std), at each checkpoint zip:
  only policy.pth's log_std is read (weights_only=True); a named
  checkpoint's step is the JSON data member's num_timesteps.
- Saturation flags and alarms found from the ledger (>= 5 episodes
  listing max_actuator_saturation_fraction flag an evaluation; two in
  a row are an alarm), marked with the given checkpoints on ten pages
  of graphs: PNGs, a self-contained HTML page and a JSON summary
  (mesozoic.training-history/v1) with the bars, the band settings and
  what was absent. A missing file or column is an absent series.
- An --out inside a run directory is refused, as plot_gate_progress.py
  refuses it.

No training, evaluation, gate, configuration, digest or notebook
change. test_policy_loading.py lists the new call-time read of
_PERIODIC_CHECKPOINT_RE, and test_repository_root.py the script's
sys.path bootstrap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
